@page "/components/separator"

<PageTitle>Separator — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Separator</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Decorative by default, as in Radix: a rule that only draws a line is noise to a screen reader,
    so it is hidden from the tree unless the caller says it separates something.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="SeparatorExample.razor"><SeparatorExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Vertical</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    It is a one-pixel box, so it needs a height from something. A row with <code>h-*</code> or
    <code>items-stretch</code> supplies it; without one the rule is there and invisible.
</p>
<Example Source="SeparatorVertical.razor"><SeparatorVertical /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Menu</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>Decorative="false"</code> gives it <code>role="separator"</code>. Inside a menu it does
    separate groups of commands, which is the case where announcing it helps rather than chatters.
</p>
<Example Source="SeparatorMenu.razor"><SeparatorMenu /></Example>

